<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>About three months of low mood, exhaustion, poor sleep with waking at three in the morning, loss of interest in singing and reading, poor appetite with 5 kg weight loss, and withdrawal from friends, in a man of 58 under sustained political pressure; PHQ-9 22 with thoughts of being better off dead; depression suspected; medical causes being excluded and urgent psychiatric consultation arranged: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Sustained political persecution: passport withheld, concerts and recordings cancelled, income lost, and surveillance by federal agencies; a major and realistic stressor, not a delusion: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Evaluation: PHQ-9, GAD-7, AUDIT-C and a cognitive screen (MoCA); blood count, metabolic panel, calcium, TSH, vitamin B12, folate, morning testosterone and hemoglobin A1c, with HIV and syphilis tests, to exclude medical causes; a review of medicines; and a sleep apnea screen. Guideline: APA Clinical Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Depression Across Three Age Cohorts (2019); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Urgent psychiatric consultation in three days to confirm the diagnosis with a structured interview, screen for bipolar disorder, judge suicide risk and the level of care, and advise on psychotherapy, medicines, and when ECT or other treatments would be indicated. Guideline: APA Clinical Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Depression Across Three Age Cohorts (2019); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); The Practice of Electroconvulsive Therapy: Recommendations for Treatment, Training, and Privileging. A Task Force Report of the American Psychiatric Association, 2nd edition (record of the American Journal of Psychiatry review, 2002) (2001) [S]</item><item>Safety: structured suicide-risk assessment, a written safety plan, no firearm in the home, medicines dispensed in limited supplies and kept locked, the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline, and a safety review at every visit. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024) [S]</item><item>Trust and equity: explain who can see his record and how it is protected; a therapist of his choosing, including a Black clinician if he wishes; treat discrimination and persecution as real stressors and record his account of surveillance as realistic; a social worker for help with income and costs; guard against the documented under-treatment of depression in Black patients by measuring response at every visit. Guideline: APA Clinical Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Depression Across Three Age Cohorts (2019); Williams DR, et al. Prevalence and distribution of major depressive disorder in African Americans, Caribbean blacks, and non-Hispanic whites: results from the National Survey of American Life. Arch Gen Psychiatry 2007;64(3):305-315 (2007); Sprenger S, et al. Retrospective Cohort Study of Racial-Ethnic Disparities in Receipt of Electroconvulsive Therapy, 2016-2021. Psychiatr Serv 2025;76(8):736-740 (2025); Racial disparities in psychotic disorder diagnosis: A review of empirical literature (2014) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
